<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="AARCH64:LE:64:v8A:default">
<!--
    kuna-relswitch: an arm64e hardened jump table (clang
    -faarch64-jump-table-hardening; Swift enum dispatch on iOS) recovered as a
    switch.  iOS 16 CryptoKit 0x1a64d6a60 rendered its tail as
    `(*(code *)(*(int *)&sub_1a64d6d7c[a1 * 4] + 0x1a64d6abc))();`.

    Source (decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/relswitch_arm64e.s):
      lsr  x16, x0, #62
      cmp  x16, #3
      csel x16, x16, xzr, ls            ; clamp, no guard branch
      adrp x17, jt ; add x17, x17, :lo12:jt
      ldrsw x16, [x17, x16, lsl #2]
      adr  x17, base ; add x16, x17, x16 ; br x16
    with the four 32-bit offsets (relative to `base`) inline after the body.
    bl targets 0x100078 (g) and 0x100084 (sink) are `ret` stand-ins.

    Stage model: P2 switch-model recovery.  The clamp makes the switch value a
    MULTIEQUAL of the index and 0, so JumpBasic finds no guard.  `switchtrim`
    then opened that unbounded value to [0, jumptablemax), read past the table
    into code, failed its sanity check, and left the computed jump.  The
    default-path model (JumpBasic2) bounds it, and is now tried before a
    trimmed basic model is accepted.  Strict fix: both passes (switchtrim on,
    the default, and off) print the same four-case switch.
-->
